      "abstract_parts": 1,
      "full_abstract_in_JSONLD_and_DC": true,
      "explicit_math_serialization": "The rank completion printed in Ohtsuki's Conjecture 7.30 cannot interpolate the standard unified sl_n invariants of an integral homology sphere with nonzero Casson invariant. A finite quotient forces its first Taylor coefficients to be affine in n, contrary to the classical cubic coefficient formula. The specified Poincaré sphere gives the incompatible values 0,−6,−24. This is a negative answer to the literal displayed statement, obtained from established quantum-invariant results.",
      "native_assets_and_Bib_exact": true,
      "canonical": "https://aleckriebel.com/research/habiro-rank-interpolation-obstruction/"
    },
    {
      "record_id": 23443039,
